NCT01234402_28220020,Progression-Free Survival (PFS) [Time Frame: From Date of Randomization until Disease Progression or Death Due to Any Cause (Up To 97 weeks)],"Of 153 patients randomized, 150 received treatment. Median PFS (95% confidence interval) was 22.1 (12.1-36.1) weeks on RAM + CAP, 7.3 (6.3-13.0) weeks on ICR + CAP, and 19.0 (12.1-24.3) weeks on CAP (hazard ratios [HRs]: 0.691, p = .1315, RAM + CAP versus CAP; 1.480, p = .0851, ICR + CAP versus CAP). Median OS was 67.4 weeks on RAM + CAP, 62.1 weeks on ICR + CAP, and 71.6 weeks on CAP (HRs: 1.833, p = .0283, RAM + CAP versus CAP; 1.468, p = .1550, ICR + CAP versus CAP). There was no statistically significant difference in PFS or OS between either combination arm and CAP. Treatment-related adverse events more frequent (by ≥10%) on RAM + CAP than on CAP were constipation, decreased appetite, headache, epistaxis, and hypertension. Those more frequent (by ≥10%) on ICR + CAP than CAP were anemia, increased lacrimation, periorbital edema, nausea, vomiting, peripheral edema, facial edema, dehydration, and dyspnea.",0.4608,53.92,llm,gpt-5.6-luna,concordant,"The registered and published primary outcomes are both PFS. Reporting median PFS and hazard ratios does not change the endpoint. The publication also reports OS and adverse events, but these are registered secondary outcomes or safety analyses rather than replacement primary endpoints. The original registry version is unavailable, so the current entry is interpreted cautiously. No registry change history is available, and the original prospective primary outcome cannot be verified. The current registry entry was used cautiously. The current PFS wording is concordant with the publication; no major switch is assigned based on the absence of the original version.",high,True,False,False,False,,0.96,Concordant (no change),clinically equivalent,"Progression-Free Survival (PFS), reported as median PFS with hazard ratios and p-values",,True,,"[{""registered_endpoint""