NCT01740427_27959613,Progression-Free Survival (PFS) as Assessed by the Investigator [Time Frame: From randomization date to date of first documentation of progression or death (up to approximately 2.5 years)],"The median progression-free survival was 24.8 months (95% confidence interval [CI], 22.1 to not estimable) in the palbociclib-letrozole group, as compared with 14.5 months (95% CI, 12.9 to 17.1) in the placebo-letrozole group (hazard ratio for disease progression or death, 0.58; 95% CI, 0.46 to 0.72; P<0.001). The most common grade 3 or 4 adverse events were neutropenia (occurring in 66.4% of the patients in the palbociclib-letrozole group vs. 1.4% in the placebo-letrozole group), leukopenia (24.8% vs. 0%), anemia (5.4% vs. 1.8%), and fatigue (1.8% vs. 0.5%). Febrile neutropenia was reported in 1.8% of patients in the palbociclib-letrozole group and in none of the patients in the placebo-letrozole group. Permanent discontinuation of any study treatment as a result of adverse events occurred in 43 patients (9.7%) in the palbociclib-letrozole group and in 13 patients (5.9%) in the placebo-letrozole group.",0.4616,53.84,llm,gpt-5.6-luna,concordant,"The registered primary outcome and published primary outcome are both progression-free survival, using progression or death as the event. Reporting median PFS and a hazard ratio does not change the endpoint. No affirmative evidence shows a different timeframe, definition, population, measurement method, or replacement of the registered primary outcome. No original/prospective registry version or change history was available. The current registry entry was used cautiously as the registered comparator, and no major switch was inferred from the current wording alone.",high,True,False,False,False,,0.98,Concordant (no change),clinically equivalent,"Progression-free survival, reported as median PFS and hazard ratio for disease progression or death, comparing palbociclib-letrozole with placebo-letrozole.",,True,,"[{""registe