NCT02401347_36253484,Objective Response (OR) [Time Frame: up to 24 weeks],"Talazoparib, a PARP inhibitor, is active in germline BRCA1 and BRCA2 (gBRCA1/2)-mutant advanced breast cancer, but its activity beyond gBRCA1/2 is poorly understood. We conducted Talazoparib Beyond BRCA ( NCT02401347 ), an open-label phase II trial, to evaluate talazoparib in patients with pretreated advanced HER2-negative breast cancer (n = 13) or other solid tumors (n = 7) with mutations in homologous recombination (HR) pathway genes other than BRCA1 and BRCA2. In patients with breast cancer, four patients had a Response Evaluation Criteria in Solid Tumors (RECIST) partial response (overall response rate, 31%), and three additional patients had stable disease of ≥6 months (clinical benefit rate, 54%). All patients with germline mutations in PALB2 (gPALB2; encoding partner and localizer of BRCA2) had treatment-associated tumor regression. Tumor or plasma circulating tumor DNA (ctDNA) HR deficiency (HRD) scores were correlated with treatment outcomes and were increased in all gPALB2 tumors. In addition, a gPALB2-associated mutational signature was associated with tumor response. Thus, talazoparib has been demonstrated to have efficacy in patients with advanced breast cancer who have gPALB2 mutations, showing activity in the context of HR pathway gene mutations beyond gBRCA1/2.",0.3536,64.64,llm,gpt-5.6-luna,concordant,"The registered Objective Response outcome and the published RECIST-based ORR are clinically equivalent. The publication does not restate the registered 24-week timeframe, but no different timeframe or endpoint definition is affirmatively reported. Clinical benefit rate is a registered secondary outcome rather than a switched or additional primary endpoint. The missing PFS secondary outcome does not constitute primary outcome switching. Registry change history was unavailable. The current registry primary outcome was used cautiously; the original prospective outcome cannot be verified, and no major switch is inferred from the current wording alone.",high,True,False,False,False,,0.94,Concordant (no change),clinically equivalent,Objective response rate (ORR) assessed by RECIST; 4 partial responses among 13 patients with breast cancer (31%),,True,,"[{""registered_endpoint"": ""Objective Response (OR) [Time Frame: up to 24 weeks]"", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""Objective response rate (ORR) by RECIST, reported as partial responses"", ""same_construct"": true, ""same_timeframe"": null, ""same_definition"": true, ""same_population"": null, ""same_measurement_method"": true, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": true, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}]",auto_accepted,confirm,concordant,True,,AUTO,,pipeline_v4.5,2026-09-06T03:10:25.379129+00:00
