NCT01989676_30568294,Objective Response Rate (ORR) Derived From Central Radiology Assessments: ITT Population [Time Frame: From the date of randomization until all participants had either completed the Week 33 tumor assessment or discontinued study drug earlier than the Week 33 visit],"The risk ratio for ORR was 0.940 (95% CI: 0.842-1.049). The 95% CI fell within the pre-specified equivalence margin of 0.80-1.25. ORR was 62.5% (95% CI: 57.2-67.6%) in the PF-05280014 group and 66.5% (95% CI: 61.3-71.4%) in the trastuzumab-EU group. As of data cut-off on 11 January 2017 (using data up to 378 days post-randomisation), there were no notable differences between groups in progression-free survival (median: 12.16 months in the PF-05280014 group vs. 12.06 months in the trastuzumab-EU group; 1-year rate: 54% vs. 51%) or overall survival (median: not reached in either group; 1-year rate: 89.31% vs. 87.36%). Safety outcomes and immunogenicity were similar between the treatment groups.",0.6428,35.72,llm,gpt-5.6-luna,concordant,"The registered and published primary outcomes are both ORR. The publication reports ORR as the principal endpoint and evaluates it using the prespecified equivalence margin. Although the provided publication text does not restate all registry qualifiers such as central radiology, ITT population, or the Week 33 assessment window, it provides no affirmative evidence that these endpoint attributes changed. Therefore, the primary endpoint is concordant and no outcome switch is identified. No registry change history is available. The current registry entry was used cautiously as the registered comparator, but the original prospective primary outcome cannot be independently confirmed.",high,True,False,False,False,,0.97,Concordant (no change),clinically equivalent,"Objective Response Rate (ORR), with equivalence assessed using the risk ratio and a prespecified equivalence margin of 0.80-1.25.",,True,,"[{""registered_endpoint"": ""Objective Response Rate (ORR) d