NCT00066690_25495490,"Disease-free Survival [Time Frame: 5-year estimates, reported at a median follow-up of 67 months.]","After a median follow-up of 67 months, the estimated disease-free survival rate at 5 years was 86.6% in the tamoxifen-ovarian suppression group and 84.7% in the tamoxifen group (hazard ratio for disease recurrence, second invasive cancer, or death, 0.83; 95% confidence interval [CI], 0.66 to 1.04; P=0.10). Multivariable allowance for prognostic factors suggested a greater treatment effect with tamoxifen plus ovarian suppression than with tamoxifen alone (hazard ratio, 0.78; 95% CI, 0.62 to 0.98). Most recurrences occurred in patients who had received prior chemotherapy, among whom the rate of freedom from breast cancer at 5 years was 82.5% in the tamoxifen-ovarian suppression group and 78.0% in the tamoxifen group (hazard ratio for recurrence, 0.78; 95% CI, 0.60 to 1.02). At 5 years, the rate of freedom from breast cancer was 85.7% in the exemestane-ovarian suppression group (hazard ratio for recurrence vs. tamoxifen, 0.65; 95% CI, 0.49 to 0.87).",0.5438,45.62,llm,gpt-5.6-luna,concordant,"The registered current primary endpoint and published primary endpoint are the same clinical outcome with the same stated timeframe and follow-up. The publication's hazard ratios, adjusted analysis, treatment comparisons, and subgroup results are analyses of disease-free survival rather than replacement endpoints. Missing secondary outcomes do not constitute primary outcome switching. Registry change history was unavailable, so the current registry primary outcome was used cautiously. The original prospective primary outcome cannot be independently confirmed, and no major switch is inferred from the current entry alone.",high,True,False,False,False,,0.98,Concordant (no change),clinically equivalent,Disease-free survival at 5 years after a median follow-up of 67 months,,True,,"[{""registered_endpoint"": ""Disease-free Survival; 5-year estimates, reported at a me