NCT00390455_25348000,"Progression-free Survival (PFS) [Time Frame: Interval from randomization until disease progression or death, whichever occurs first, assessed up to 5 years]","At the third planned interim analysis, the futility boundary was crossed, and the data and safety monitoring board recommend study closure, having accrued 295 patients. At the final analysis, there was no difference in PFS (hazard ratio [HR] of placebo to lapatinib, 1.04; 95% CI, 0.82 to 1.33; P = .37); median PFS was 4.7 months for fulvestrant plus lapatinib versus 3.8 months for fulvestrant plus placebo. There was no difference in overall survival (OS) (HR, 0.91; 95% CI, 0.68 to 1.21; P = .25). For HER2-normal tumors, median PFS did not differ by treatment arm (4.1 v 3.8 months). For HER2-positive tumors, lapatinib was associated with longer median PFS (5.9 v 3.3 months), but the differential treatment effect by HER2 status was not significant (P = .53). The most frequent toxicities were diarrhea, fatigue, and rash associated with lapatinib.",0.4974,50.26,llm,gpt-5.6-luna,concordant,"The registered primary endpoint available for assessment is PFS, and the publication reports PFS as its primary outcome. The publication also reports OS, which was a registered secondary outcome, and subgroup PFS analyses, which do not constitute new or switched endpoints. The publication does not restate every registered timeframe or definition detail, but it provides no affirmative evidence of a different endpoint. Registry change history was unavailable, so only the current registry entry could be assessed. The original prospective primary outcome cannot be confirmed, and no major switch is inferred from the current wording alone.",high,True,False,False,False,,0.98,Concordant (no change),clinically equivalent,"Progression-free survival (PFS), evaluated at the final analysis and reported using hazard ratio and median PFS.",,True,,"[{""registered_endpoint"": ""Progression-free Survival (PFS): interval from